**5. Illustrative Application: Pathfinding on a Grid**

To demonstrate the behavior of the Resonance-Guided Metric, we applied it to a simple pathfinding problem on a 2D grid. Each cell $(r,c)$ in the grid was assigned a configuration value $x_{cell} = \text{mod}((r \cdot 0.1 + c \cdot 0.05) \cdot X_{max}, X_{max})$, mapping grid positions to the input $x$ of the $A(x,d_{res})$ function (with $x_0=0$). We used an A\* search algorithm, comparing paths found using a standard Manhattan distance ($d_{base}=1$ for adjacent cells) against paths found using $d_{RGM}$ with $f_{mod}$ as defined in Section 3.1 ($w=2.0$) and $N_{ord}=\{1,...,12\}$.

